  "solution": {
    "approach": "Calculate the product of all digits of an integer.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(D)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    char s[1005]; if (scanf(\"%s\", s) != 1) return 0;\n    long long prod = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; s[i]; i++) prod *= (s[i] - '0');\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", prod);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    string s; if (!(cin >> s)) return 0;\n    long long prod = 1;\n    for (char c : s) prod *= (c - '0');\n    cout << prod << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNext()) {\n            String s = sc.next();\n            long prod = 1;\n            for (char c : s.toCharArray()) prod *= (c - '0');\n            System.out.println(prod);\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\ndef main():\n    toks = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not toks: return\n    prod = 1\n    for c in toks[0]: prod *= int(c)\n    print(prod)\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require(\"fs\");\nfunction main() {\n    const toks = fs.readFileSync(0, \"utf-8\").trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (!toks || !toks[0]) return;\n    let prod = 1n;\n    for (const c of toks[0]) prod *= BigInt(c);\n    console.log(prod.toString());\n}\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Iterate through each digit of the number and multiply into accumulator."
  },
